WEBVTT

00:00:00.641 --> 00:00:12.641
Curves: first trace the real head. The machine's head exists only as a triangle mesh (STL)—new file, File → Import the head mesh

00:00:14.194 --> 00:00:24.090
The head casting, with access windows all round. We only want its outer shape—the upper box. Make the mesh semi-transparent so we can trace behind it

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:31.040
New sketch, orientation XZ plane (the head's side, seen from the front)

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:40.742
Polyline: click along the mesh outline—bottom left, bottom right, top right, to where the top starts to curve at the front

00:00:40.742 --> 00:00:52.742
The front-top corner is a smooth curve: use the interpolating B-spline—it passes through every point you click. From the end of the top edge, click 6 points along the mesh to the end of the left edge

00:00:53.990 --> 00:01:05.000
The side outline is closed: lines plus one B-spline. A traced outline needn't be fully constrained; it just has to follow the mesh closely
